{
	title: 'Host facts use durable notices, never tool output',
	spec: 'Resource warnings, neighbor edit activity and host restarts reach models as Hal notices at the first subsequent request through history.messages and model-notices. They never start or resume turns. Bash results contain only tool output and failures, with no host-fact suffixes. A host-only notice history record stores original time and factual text; delivery freezes on existing notice-only user records, using existing replay, prompt-edit and context-boundary rules. Preserve resource thresholds, client warnings, recovery warnings and critical turn pausing. Resource notices describe level transitions including recovery, not each sample. Neighbor activity stays bounded to open same-cwd sessions, the existing recent window and path limit, sampled before model requests rather than bash results; changed facts are told once. Host startup stores the loaded version; restored open sessions learn that a new host started, with the previous loaded version when known and deliberate attribution when available, otherwise cause unknown, before recovery requests. First startup is not called a restart; local client restarts do not announce host restarts. Keep existing client restart warnings without a new UI divider. Remove obsolete suffix functions and redundant delivery state. Tests cover notice-only scheduling, intact tool results, first-request delivery and durable replay, resource recovery and restart facts. No durable second queue or per-request scan of all histories.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Restored invariant: tool results retain their actual output and failures; Hal facts reach the next model request even when the model never runs bash. Resource and neighbor suffix functions and bash imports are removed, not retained as compatibility paths. Existing notice freezing, replay, compaction and prompt ownership supply delivery; no second queue.',
		'Startup runs under the host lock before opening the socket: otherwise a reconnecting client can request input before its restart fact is recorded. The bounded restart live file retains loaded version plus any deliberate cause, consumed at startup. Unknown cause means unknown, not an invented crash. Emergency restart reports persistence failures on stderr and still exits; ordinary startup corruption throws with the path.',
		'Critical resource pausing remains in a finally block around notice persistence, so ENOSPC cannot bypass the stop. New or reopened sessions bootstrap the current shortage at request assembly; weak metadata identities avoid retaining closed sessions. Neighbor path/fingerprint pruning bounds idle accumulation, while active counters survive expiry so old background completions cannot finish newer activity.',
		'Independent review found two safety edges and both are fixed: one unreadable restored tab reports its full startup-notice error without blocking other tabs or listening; critical pressure failure-isolates every stop and aborts each controller even when form dismissal or pause persistence fails. Startup errors remain available to newly connecting clients, not only a transient toast. Critical stop closes questions rather than treating cancellation as a skip.',
		'Validation: 67 affected tests pass; TypeScript and changed-file lint pass. An unchanged read-only baseline and the initial integration run fail the same six full-suite cases: import-old tool header, SIGUSR1 hangup, terminal module line limit, and three browser layout cases. Later concurrent runs are not comparable because other sessions are changing shared files. Final integration is checked from this task commit in a read-only worktree. Live delivery was observed after another session restarted: both the attributed host restart and subsequent neighbor changes arrived as meta text without bash.'
